1.fork()	Creates a new child process
2.exec()	Executes the Linux command in the child process
3.wait()	Makes the parent wait until the child finishes
4.getpid()	Returns the current process ID
5.getppid()	Returns the parent process ID
6.read()	Reads the command entered by the user

1.uname	  Displays operating system and kernel information
2.lscpu	  Displays CPU architecture and processor information
3.lsblk	  Displays storage devices and block devices
4.ps	    Displays information about running processes
5.top    	Displays real-time process and system resource usage

